  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_005 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.6501 acc. RNA clearly dominates image (0.48-0.65 vs 0.21 for resnet50 image-only), and avgpool beats transformer for aggregation. However, we have not yet tested whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs the weak resnet50) combined with the best RNA pipeline could push accuracy above 0.65. Question: Does adding image features from a pretrained ViT-L to the already-optimized scvi_n200/multiprofile/avgpool RNA pipeline improve validation accuracy via simple concat fusion? Why this experiment: config_036 isolates the effect of adding a potentially informative image modality to the best RNA configuration, using the simplest fusion (concat) to avoid confounding. It is the highest-potential untested configuration that could beat the current best. If it succeeds, the remaining 3 experiments can refine fusion (weighted) or aggregation (transformer); if it fails, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can spend remaining budget on minor RNA-only variants."
}

